@startuml 03-sequence-jwt-auth
title JWT sign-in and refresh
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #4F46E5
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #C7D2FE
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF2FF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #4F46E5
skinparam ParticipantFontStyle bold
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #EEF2FF
skinparam ActorBorderColor #4F46E5
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #EEF2FF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #4F46E5
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam NoteBorderColor #F59E0B
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam SequenceGroupHeaderFontColor #334155
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #E0E7FF
skinparam SequenceDividerBorderColor #4F46E5
skinparam TitleFontSize 18

actor User
participant "Web app" as Web
participant "API" as API
database "Database" as DB

== Sign in ==
User -> Web : enter API key or operator token
Web -> API : POST /auth/token
API -> DB : save refresh token (hashed)
API --> Web : access token (15 min)\n+ refresh cookie (7 days)

== Use the app ==
Web -> API : request + Bearer access token
API --> Web : data

== Refresh (automatic) ==
Web -> API : POST /auth/refresh (cookie)
API -> DB : use old token, save new one
API --> Web : new access token + new cookie

== Sign out ==
User -> Web : Sign out
Web -> API : POST /auth/logout
API -> DB : revoke the session
API --> Web : cookie cleared

note over API, DB
  A refresh token works once. If an old one is used
  again, the whole session is revoked.
end note
@enduml
